onal annotation, and multiple association tests. The central claim is that leveraging variant characteristics through fast, accurate INLA estimation enables BATI to outperform existing methods on realistic cohorts. The study highlights that differences between methods are most pronounced at low variance-explained levels, where some methods show near-zero power. Overall, the paper advances both methodology and practical application, offering a flexible testing approach that can be extended in future work.",
